{
 "id": "260-29",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "One of my key expectations is that you don't use a notebook for taking notes.",
  "Notebooks can become a crutch, encouraging shallow engagement and passive learning.",
  "Instead, I want you to develop the habit of active learning and deep understanding.",
  "Use our internal tools and version control systems to document your work.",
  "This way, your thoughts are organized, searchable, and accessible to the entire team.",
  "It also ensures that your knowledge isn't locked away in a private notebook.",
  "I recommend using our internal wiki and knowledge base.",
  "You can create pages for each project or topic, and then use headers, links, and even code blocks to structure your notes.",
  "Consistency is key when multiple people are contributing to the same knowledge base.",
  "We have a style guide that outlines our preferred formatting, including how to structure headings, when to use bold or italics, and how to properly format code blocks.",
  "For now, just focus on adapting to this new style.",
  "Remember, the goal is to cultivate a habit of documenting your work in a structured, accessible manner.",
  "I want you to use Discord from now on.",
  "It's a great tool for team collaboration, and most of our colleagues are already active on it.",
  "For now, just make sure you're regularly online and responsive.",
  "We can discuss specific channel setups and rules later.",
  "It's crucial that you always include try statements in your functions."
 ],
 "admitted": 17,
